WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
[QUIET MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.150
Hi.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.230
I'm Andrea.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:45.665
I am a second-year master
student at the Media Lab.

00:00:45.665 --> 00:00:47.350
And so this is some of my work.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.150
My work ranges from
wearable sculpture

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.630
to large-scale public
art installations.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.337
And I'm now working in a lab
that designs from the micro

00:00:59.337 --> 00:01:03.680
to macro scale, using tools
that work with nature.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.370
My name is Nicolas
Kisic Aguirre.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.127
I'm a recent graduate
of the ACT program,

00:01:15.127 --> 00:01:16.710
so that's Art, Culture
and Technology.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.350
It's basically the visual
arts program at MIT.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.030
Although it's all
about visual studies,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.940
my concentration or my focus has
been over the past three years

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.110
in sound.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:31.860
I try to understand how
sound effects public space

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.310
and how public spaces are space
for [? politics. ?] To have

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.243
a perspective in
this, I make machines,

00:01:37.243 --> 00:01:38.910
and these machines
end up being my tools

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.850
to have a voice in
the construction

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.650
of the sonic soundscape.

00:01:49.865 --> 00:01:50.365
Hi.

00:01:50.365 --> 00:01:51.640
So I'm Brian Huang.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.850
I'm a senior majoring in
computer science and finance.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.645
There's a industrial
[INAUDIBLE] dress that I made.

00:01:58.645 --> 00:02:02.230
It was inspired mostly by like
a sense of a nebulous future

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.140
and what could be coming
after undergraduate, which is

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.940
kind of where I am right now.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.389
Well, I have my second show on
the [INAUDIBLE] Room at MIT.

00:02:10.389 --> 00:02:13.830
It featured six looks,
four womenswear looks

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.160
and two menswear looks.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.460
And basically it was a
progression from youthfulness

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.379
into sort of unclear
future and adulthood.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.100
My name is Gary Zhexi Zhang.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.840
I'm a graduate student in the
first year of the Art, Culture,

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.110
Technology program.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.010
In my work, I'm predominantly
a filmmaker and a writer.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.190
And the films that
I'm presenting here

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.560
were made over the
past couple of years

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.960
on a number of different themes
between politics of identity

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.660
and authenticity
in Chinese history,

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.170
but also on the intersection
of contemporary technology

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.260
and biology.

